#### Interview Cheat Sheet 🎯

*** Definition: “Inheritance is a mechanism where a derived class acquires properties and behavior of a base class.”
*** Keyword used: : (colon) with access specifier — class Derived : public Base
*** 5 Types: Single, Multiple, Multilevel, Hierarchical, Hybrid
*** Private members are NEVER inherited directly — remember this rule!
*** Constructor order: Base class constructor runs first, then Derived
*** C++ supports Multiple Inheritance (unlike Java, jo interfaces use karta hai iske liye)
*** Diamond Problem: Multiple inheritance mein ek issue aata hai jab do base classes same grandparent class se inherit karti hain — isse solve karte hain virtual inheritance se